{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>Only the gold.</b> Even though the vessels were purified from corpse-impurity, they still require care regarding gentile rust — to boil them out (lehag'il) and to purge the vessels of the grease of their carrion absorbed within. And our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted the word אך to mean that the metal should be as it is: this teaches that one must remove its rust before boiling it out."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:37:21.108906506Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}